{title: How Firm a Foundation}
{artist: John Rippon's Selection}
{key: G}
{time: 2/2}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
How [G]firm a foun[C]dation, ye [G]saints of the [D]Lord,
is [G]laid for your [C]faith in his [G]excellent [D]word!
What [G]more can he [C]say than to [G]you he hath [D]said —
to [G]you who for [C]refuge to [G]Jesus have [D]fled?

Verse 2
In [G]every condition, [C]in [G]sickness, in [D]health;
in [G]poverty's vale, [C]or abounding [G]in [D]wealth;
at [G]home and abroad, [C]on the [G]land, on the [D]sea,
as [G]thy days demand, [C]shall thy [G]strength ever [D]be.

Verse 3
Fear [G]not, I am [C]with thee, [G]O be not [D]dismayed,
for [G]I am thy God, [C]and will still give [G]thee [D]aid;
I'll [G]strengthen and help [C]thee, and [G]cause thee to [D]stand,
upheld [G]by my [C]righteous, [G]omnipotent [D]hand.

Verse 4
When [G]through the deep [C]waters I [G]call thee to [D]go,
the [G]rivers of woe [C]shall not [G]thee [D]overflow;
for [G]I will be [C]with thee, [G]thy troubles to [D]bless,
and [G]sanctify to [C]thee thy [G]deepest [D]distress.

Verse 5
When [G]through fiery [C]trials thy [G]pathways shall [D]lie,
my [G]grace, all sufficient, [C]shall be [G]thy [D]supply;
the [G]flame shall [C]not hurt thee; [G]I only [D]design
thy [G]dross to consume, [C]and thy [G]gold to [D]refine.
